From 6acbef62472feac3b785e00102b04c87c8acec33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roi Blum <roiblum05@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:10:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat: a nodepool may draw Agents from several InfraEnvs
 (additionalInfraEnvNames)

nodepool[].additionalInfraEnvNames lists more InfraEnvs a NodePool may take
Agents from. With it, the agentLabelSelector is one matchExpressions
requirement, infraenvs.agent-install.openshift.io In (infraEnvName plus the
list, sorted and unique); without it, the single matchLabels it always was,
so every existing cluster file renders exactly as before (the golden tests
still pass).

The NodePool's name still derives from infraEnvName alone, so adding or
removing an InfraEnv never renames it. On an InPlace NodePool a changed
selector touches no running node; on Replace it rolls every node.

The render fails on KubeVirt (a VM pool draws from no InfraEnv), with the
legacy agentLabelSelector.nodeLabelKey (it names one label, not a set), on a
value that is not a list, and on an entry that is not a name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016gPPBP4UxCerc81DKaJHKm
